  "decision": "v1.5 (2026-08-14). IN_PLAY_SHAPE_SLOPE = 1.10 \u2014 the only model value moved.\n\nWHAT AND WHY. _recal_shape was skipped once rounds posted, so in-play shipped at an effective s=1.00 that no measurement ever chose \u2014 skipping the recal was never no-opinion. Fitted through _recal_shape own sum-preserving contract on inplay_calib.npz, train pre-2026, scored on the untouched 2026 holdout: mean LL 0.138938 -> 0.13874, event-clustered 95% CI [-0.00060, -0.00013], P(gain) 0.999, and all three in-play stages improve.\n\nWHY 1.10 AND NOT MORE. The LL surface is flat over [1.05, 1.225], so the argmin is not identified; 1.10 is interior to the train flat region AND is the holdout argmin \u2014 the one value both splits pick. 1.25 and 1.30 are actively WORSE than doing nothing on holdout. A single global constant BEAT both per-stage and per-stage-per-market out of sample, so the extra parameters were rejected rather than shipped.\n\nSCOPE. Pre-tournament path proven BIT-IDENTICAL (max |old-new| = 0.000000000000). _recal_rank stays OFF in-play: RANK_OFFSETS were fitted pre-tournament and have never been measured in-play, and stacking an unmeasured correction under a measured one is how a defect hides. Effect is ~0.2-0.3% of log-loss \u2014 a sharpness fix, NOT an edge. Do not size any bet off it.\n\nALSO REJECTED THIS PASS, recorded so they are not re-proposed: HALF_LIFE_D 90 vs 270 \u2014 270 wins 8/8 on train and 6/8 on the 2026 holdout, with top20 LL +0.0059 against it, so 270 STAYS and the separate recent-form term is moot with it. Course fit stays out: 74% of it survives a course-key placebo, i.e. it is form wearing a venue label. The wave tilt needed no change \u2014 it is already applied live via pga_wave.wave_shift_for, and its 36-hole net is -0.023 str/rnd (z=-0.43) because wave labels flip R1->R2 for 97.1% of players.\n\nNON-MODEL CHANGES in the same pass (no constants): golf_collect now strips FanDuel name padding and refuses market-group labels in the event column (85% of rows were padded, 12.3% carried a market name); the tee harvester covers Korn Ferry and Champions (+333 gradeable closes). G2 unchanged and still FAILING its placebo arm.",
